Z||000000||Philphine||05-01-2001||01:35 PM||||<BR>no...raffle tickets aren't being offered. i've pretty much decided to give or sell very cheap (couple hundred bucks) to my nephew my cheap thrill fiero. i've only got a few hundred dollars in it and it'll just siphon off cash for other projects. i've talked to my brother (his nephew also. my older sisters grandson), who works with kids and he said to try to tie it in with his grades and finding a part time job. i'm also hoping he'll take some interest in trying to repair it. a couple of things would need to be done before he could drive it anyway. i think i can fix them both (brakes and mysterious battery drain), but if i give it to him i want him in on the repair. i used to hit the thrift stores and build my  nieces and nephews bikes that they fairly promtly distroyed. then i got the boys tools which never got used at all that i know of. hopefully a car would be more of an inspiration to ty some repair. he's 15 anyway so there would be plenty of time do get it driveable before he can really use it.   <P>aother reason i want to give it to him is because he has a cousin a few years older that was in a fairly serious accident and got a pretty hefty settlement (lost an arm). of course being young when he was old enough he got himself a new car. i'm not really trying to do an in family "keeping up with the jones", but i thought while i am able this time i could help him drive too. i'm not from a particulaly well to do family. <P>a sort of problem with this is they each have younger brothers. as they come of age i don't think i'll be in this position again to help them get cars too. i'd have to try and explain that i probaly can't help them too (probaly won't matter as much with the brother of the nephew that had the accident).<P>haven't told him yet. still need to talk to his mother (my niece, i can't see her not wanting him to have it) and try to make sure i think it through as well as possible. part of me knows this could be a waste of a nice little car. not that he's a bad kid (in avanced classes in one of the harder to get into magnet schools). i've just never seen much mechanical interest.  <P>whaddaya think? am i covering all the bases?       <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (parts car or project. time will tell)||||reg||1
